2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Valborg (Berge) Solovskoy, 87, passed away on April 29, 2005 in Hopkins, MN. Born to Rev. Matthias Jacob and Inga (Grangaard) Berge on May 7, 1917 in Wildrose, ND, Valborg was confirmed in the Lutheran faith, graduated from Underw
2 CONC ood (MN) High School and Concordia College, Moorhead, MN, with a Bachelor of Arts degree in English. Valborg taught junior high school English in Sacramento, CA and later in Edina and Wayzata, MN, and earned a masters degree in En
2 CONC glish Literature from Mankato State University. Valborg married Lt. Col. George Solovskoy on March 24, 1945. Valborg was active in teachers organizations and in her church, Westwood Lutheran, St. Louis Park, MN. Preceding her in d
2 CONC eath were her husband; a son, George Paul Solovskoy, Jr.; her parents; sisters, Helene (Berge) Ekse, Margaret (Berge) Anderson and Eunice (Berge) Stein Clauson. She is survived by a son, Matthew & wife Dorothy Solovskoy, Bilton, S
2 CONC C; six grandchildren; 15 great grandchildren; a brother, Johan & wife Myra Berge, Mound, MN; two nephews and two nieces; daughters-in-law, Helen Cole, Largo, FL, and Cindy Solovskoy, Palm Springs, CA.
2 CONT
