2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary provided by Contributor Margie Deutsch (47967793):
2 CONT Eunice Berge Clauson, 75, of Plymouth and formerly of Underwood, died Friday, June 9, 1995. She was born June 11, 1921 in Wildrose, N.D., the daughter of Rev. Mathias J. and Inga G. Berge. In 1929 she moved with her family to Unde
2 CONC rwood where she attended school. Following her high school graduation, she attended Concordia College in Moorhead and the University of Minnesota. After graduating in 1942, Eunice taught in Minnesota high schools for 17 years, fol
2 CONC lowed by 18 years as a health claims adjustor at General Mills.
2 CONT In 1944 she married Archie Stein, a lieutenant in the Army Air Corps, who was killed in action in WWII. She later married Victor Clauson, a teaching colleague and World War II veteran.
2 CONT Survivors include a brother, Johan (Myra) Berge of Mound, two sister, Margaret Anderson of Minnetonka and Valborg Solovsky of Hopkins and six nieces and nephews.
2 CONT Funeral services were held June 9 at the Lutheran Church of St. Phillip the Deacon in Plymouth.
2 CONT Published June 30, 1995, Fergus Falls Daily Journal
2 CONT
