2 CONT Matthew John Solovskoy, age 60, husband of Dorothy Crocker Solovskoy of Belton, SC, died Saturday, January 19, 2008 at the Rainey Hospice House in Anderson. Born in Fukuoka, Japan on July 19, 1947, Mr. Solovskoy was a son of the l
2 CONC ate George Solovskoy and Valborg Berge Solovskoy. He served two tours in the United States Marine Corps (3rd RECON) during the Vietnam War. He was stationed in Khe-Sanh, Hue, Phubai, and Laos. He was a graduate of North Hennipin C
2 CONC ollege in Minnesota with a degree in criminal justice. He is survived by his wife, Dorothy Crocker Solovskoy of the home, daughters, Bianca Dyar of Belton, SC, and Bethany Garcia of California and sons, Joshua Solovskoy of Virgini
2 CONC a, and Jacob Solovskoy of California. He is also survived by fifteen grandchildren. In addition to his parents, he was predeceased by his brother, Paul Solovskoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published by Anderson Independent-Mail on Jan. 21, 2008.
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT PVT US MARINE CORPS VIETNAM
2 CONT Loving husband, father and papa
