1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/149250531/katherine-laverne-fristad
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine LaVerne King Fristad BIRTH	4 Dec 1885 Waterloo, Black Hawk County, Iowa, USA DEATH	12 May 1952 (aged 66) Rockford, Winnebago County, Illinois, USA BURIAL	 Springdale Cemetery and Mausoleum Peoria, Peoria County, Illinois
2 CONC , USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Albert Fristad 1885–1945
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Lauren D. Bentley 1911–1974
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1920, married to William Bentley and living in Rockford with William and children: Bryant (1907), Lauren (1911) and Elizabeth (1916). Second wife of Albert Fristad. In 1930, this blended family was living in Rockford, IL, inclu
2 CONC ding children: Arthur, Alma, Victor, and Ada Fristad, and Lauren, Elizabeth Bentley Ocepeck and Zack/Jack (1921) Bentley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary Mrs. Katherine LaVerne Fristad, 66, former resident of Peoria, died Monday at the home of her son, Jack E. Bentley, 521 N. Avon St., Rockford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at Waterloo, Ia., Dec. 4, 1885, a daughter of Julian and Elizabeth Bryant King, she married Albert O. Fristad in Chicago. He died in Peoria in 1945.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are two sons, Jack E. Bentley at whose home she died, and Lauren D. Bentley of Peoria; one daughter, Mrs. Elizabeth Ocepeck of Chicago; three step-sons, Victor Fristad of the Navy, Arnold Fristad of Compton, Cal., and Ar
2 CONC thur Fristad of Kewanee; a step-daughter, Mrs. Alma Olson of Rockford; two sisters, Mrs. Jennie Patton of Rockford, and Mrs. Blanche Hartman of Detroit, Mich.; and one brother, Harley King of Rock Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT One son, three sisters, and two brothers are dead.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial will be in Springdale Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Full obit in the Peoria Journal, Tues., May 13, 1952, page B-5.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary located by Mel Slane and transcribed by Stephen Cantrell.
