1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eagle Grove - Eleanor R. Jacobson
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor Rebekah Jacobson the daughter of Ole and Bertha Marie (Ogland) Carlson, was born April 22, 1918, in Kanawha, Iowa. She was raised and educated in the area of her birth.
2 CONT
2 CONT On February 14, 1942, Eleanor was united in marriage with Bennie C. Jacobson in Clarion, Iowa. The couple made their home in Eagle Grove where Eleanor was a member of Samuel Lutheran Church, Priscilla Circle, American Legion Auxil
2 CONC iary and the Senior Citizens Center. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor passed away on Saturday, March 5, 2011, at Trinity Regional Medical Center in Fort Dodge, at the age of 92 years. She was preceded in death by her parents; her husband, Bennie on June 26, 1972; daughter, Ruby Ann Nelson; s
2 CONC on-in-law, Vance Nelson; sisters, Hilma Thompson and her husband Tilbert, Myra Birkland and husband Marion and Shirley Olson and brothers, Tilman Carlson and wife Nellie, Gordon, Robert and Birdsall Carlson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her granddaughters, Angela Wesselink and husband Kent of Eagle Grove and Michelle Sunner and husband Chad of Cedar Rapids; five great-grandchildren: Jacob, Benjamin and Cael Wesselink and Lucas and Sophia Sunner;
2 CONC  two sisters: Clarice Thompson and husband Burdette of Clarion and Ruby McCormick of Sioux Falls, SD; sisters-in-law: Meri Carlson and Clarice Carlson of Britt, Dorothy Buss of Mason City, Beverly Jacobson and Mabel Odland of Eagl
2 CONC e Grove; brother-in-law, Orville Olson and numerous nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Tuesday, March 8, 2011, 2:00 p.m. at Evangelical Lutheran Church in Eagle Grove with Pastor Richard Taylor officiating. Burial will be in Rose Hill Cemetery in Eagle Grove.
