1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Clarice H. (Carlson) Thompson  December 2, 1916 - July 6, 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarice H. Thompson, 94, of Clarion, Iowa, passed away July 6, 2011, at the Rehabilitation Center of Belmond, Iowa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarice Harriet Carlson, daughter of Ole and Bertha (Ogland) Carlson, was born December 2, 1916, at Kanawha, Iowa. She was baptized in the St. John’s Lutheran Church in Kanawha, Iowa, and also attended school in Norway Township. C
2 CONC larice married Burdette Thompson on November 22, 1941, in the bride’s home. Together they raised three daughters in Clarion. Clarice had been a member of Holmes Lutheran Church since 1926 (84 years). She enjoyed serving in many ar
2 CONC eas during her time there, including playing in the string band, singing in the church choir, teaching Sunday School, serving as a member of Holmes Circle for many years, and participating in Luther League. She also encouraged her
2 CONC  daughters’ by supporting their many 4-H activities over the years. Clarice was an avid gardener. In her later years, she loved uncovering hidden treasures at local auctions and antique stores.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarice is survived by her daughters: Charlotte (Chuck) Kern of Clarion, Iowa, Elaine (Fred) Hollaus of Redlands, California and Helen (Dennis) Dorenkamp of Peoria, Arizona; eight grandchildren: Angela (Shawn) Brown, Chad (Karla) 
2 CONC Kern, Dana (Kyle) Campbell, Lora (Jason) Bowman, Brent (Diana) Dorenkamp, Clinton (Jennifer) Dorenkamp, Kristine (Ryan) Klima and, Rachel (B.K.) Grayson; thirteen great-grandchildren: Norah Brown, Brayden and Caleb Kern, Emma and 
2 CONC Maddie Bowman, Chasya, Santrielle, and Kemuel Dorenkamp, Gabriel, Gavin and Makel Klima, Avery Dorenkamp and Ethan LaBounty, and Owen Grayson; and sister Ruby McCormick. Clarice was preceded in death by her husband Burdette; and s
2 CONC iblings Hilma Thompson, Tilman Carlson, Myra Birkland, Eleanor Jacobsen, Birdsell Carlson, Shirley Olson, Gordon Carlson, and Robert Carlson.
